# The relative Proj of an algebraic space is quasi-compact under finite generation

In Situation 0849 let `π : Proj_X(𝒜) ⟶ X` be the relative homogeneous spectrum of Stacks 084C,
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.RelativeProjSituation.π`.
This file proves Stacks 084F: `π` is quasi-compact if `𝒜` is of finite type as an `𝒜₀`-algebra,
or is generated over `𝒜₀` by a finite type `𝒜₀`-module `𝒜₁`, or has locally nilpotent positive
part modulo a finite type `𝒜₀`-submodule of `𝒜₊`.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.RelativeProjSituation.isQuasiCompact_π`: **Stacks 084F.**

## Implementation notes

Each of the three conditions is a condition on a quasi-coherent graded algebra which is local on
the base, so on an algebraic space it is read étale locally: it holds for the restriction `g^*𝒜`
of `𝒜` at every étale scheme point `g : T ⟶ X`
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.RelativeProjSituation.HoldsAtEtalePoints`). The restriction is the one
of Stacks 084B, `s.relativeProjPoints.algebra`, built from the re-presentation of `𝒜` with
sections in the universe of the schemes, which is identified with `𝒜` degreewise and
sectionwise by `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.RelativeProjSituation.smallAlgebraEquiv`.

The proof is the source's: by Stacks 084B the base change of `π` along a surjective étale scheme
point `g` of `X` is `Proj_T(g^*𝒜) ⟶ T`, which is quasi-compact by the case of schemes (Stacks
07ZX, `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjBridge.SheafGradedAlgebra.quasiCompact_toBase`), and
quasi-compactness is étale local on the target (Stacks 03KG,
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.RelativeProjPoints.isQuasiCompact_of_etalePoint`).

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 084F](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/084F)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 084B](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/084B)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03KG](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03KG)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07ZX](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07ZX)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjBridge

universe u m

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Space.RelativeProjSituation

variable (s : RelativeProjSituation.{u, m})

/-- **Stacks 084F.** In Situation 0849 the structure morphism `π : Proj_X(𝒜) ⟶ X` is
quasi-compact if, étale locally on `X`, one of the following holds: `𝒜` is of finite type as an
`𝒜₀`-algebra; `𝒜` is generated by `𝒜₁` as an `𝒜₀`-algebra and `𝒜₁` is a finite type
`𝒜₀`-module; there is a finite type `𝒜₀`-submodule `ℱ ⊆ 𝒜₊` such that `𝒜₊/ℱ𝒜` is a locally
nilpotent sheaf of ideals of `𝒜/ℱ𝒜`. Each condition holds at every étale point exactly when it
holds at one surjective étale point (`holdsAtEtalePoints_isFiniteTypeOverDegreeZero_iff` and its
siblings in `StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.RelativeProjPoint.EtaleLocalConditions`). -/
@[stacks 084F]
theorem isQuasiCompact_π
    (h : s.HoldsAtEtalePoints SheafGradedAlgebra.IsFiniteTypeOverDegreeZero ∨
      s.HoldsAtEtalePoints SheafGradedAlgebra.IsFinitelyGeneratedInDegreeOne ∨
      s.HoldsAtEtalePoints SheafGradedAlgebra.HasNilpotentPositiveQuotient) :
    IsQuasiCompact s.site s.base s.containsBase s.π.hom := by
  obtain ⟨T, g, hgEt, hgSurj⟩ := s.relativeProjPoints.exists_etalePoint s.space.2
  refine s.relativeProjPoints.isQuasiCompact_of_etalePoint
    s.isAlgebraicSpace_relativeProjFunctor s.space.2 T g hgEt hgSurj
    ((s.relativeProjPoints.algebra T g).quasiCompact_toBase ?_)
  rcases h with h | h | h
  · exact Or.inl (h T g hgEt)
  · exact Or.inr (Or.inl (h T g hgEt))
  · exact Or.inr (Or.inr (h T g hgEt))

end AlgebraicGeometry.Space.RelativeProjSituation

end
